            <ArticleTitle>Clinical follow-up of a woman with diffuse coronary ectasia and coronaro-left ventricular fistulae.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>273-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The presence in the same clinical case of diffuse coronary artery ectasia and multiple congenital coronary artery fistulae draining into the left ventricle is a very rare condition. Herein we report the 20-year follow-up of an 85-year old woman, in order to show that the long-term prognosis in such a double disorder is good.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
